---
// Grounded in real, verified facts, not boilerplate — see the 2026-09-07
// deep-research pass behind this page: the ICO's actual "right to be
// informed" checklist (only the items that genuinely apply to this site
// are included below; DPO contact, third-country transfers, automated
// decision-making, and consent-withdrawal are all correctly omitted
// because none of them apply here), Vercel's own stated Analytics/Speed
// Insights retention window, and the real Art 6(1)(f) legitimate-interest
// basis this project actually relies on. Unlike /methodology, this page
// is proactively linked from the footer (see SiteFooter.astro) — the ICO
// is explicit that merely having a privacy page online, unlinked, does
// not satisfy the "easily accessible" requirement.
import Logo from '../components/Logo.astro';
import PreferenceControls from '../components/PreferenceControls.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { isFlagEnabled } from '../lib/featureFlags.js';

const devModeEnabled = isFlagEnabled(import.meta.env.ENABLE_DEV_MODE);
---

<Layout
  title="daily-dose — privacy"
  description="What daily-dose actually collects, why, and for how long — a short, honest privacy notice, not boilerplate."
  path="/privacy"
>
  <header class="masthead">
    <div class="masthead-utility">
      <nav class="site-nav"><a href="/">&larr; Back to digest</a></nav>
      <PreferenceControls devModeEnabled={devModeEnabled} />
    </div>
    <hgroup class="masthead-brand">
      <h1><Logo /> Privacy</h1>
      <p class="tagline">
        This is a personal, open-source project. Here is exactly what it collects,
        why, and for how long — nothing more than that.
      </p>
    </hgroup>
  </header>

  <main>
    <h2 class="section-heading">What this site does not do</h2>
    <p>
      daily-dose has no user accounts, no sign-up, no comments, and no forms. It sets
      no cookies of its own — the light/dark theme toggle is stored only in your
      browser's <code>localStorage</code>, never sent to any server, and is not
      personal data.
    </p>

    <h2 class="section-heading">What is collected, and why</h2>
    <p>
      This site uses Vercel Web Analytics and Vercel Speed Insights to understand
      whether anyone actually reads this hobby project and whether pages load
      acceptably fast. Neither tool uses cookies or writes anything to your browser —
      visitors aren't individually identified or tracked across visits.
    </p>
    <p>Per page view, Vercel Web Analytics records: the page URL, referrer, a coarse
      geolocation (country/region/city, derived from IP address — the IP address
      itself is not retained), device type, and browser/OS. Vercel Speed Insights
      separately records real-world page-load performance (Core Web Vitals) tied to
      a route and country, not to any individual visitor.
    </p>
    <p>
      The lawful basis for this is a <strong>legitimate interest</strong> (UK
      GDPR/GDPR Art. 6(1)(f)): understanding traffic to a hobby project. This is
      genuinely the only purpose — there is no advertising, no resale of data, and no
      profiling of individual visitors.
    </p>

    <h2 class="section-heading">Who processes it</h2>
    <p>
      Vercel Inc., the host of this site, is the only third party involved. See{' '}
      <a href="https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Vercel's Web Analytics privacy documentation</a>
      {' '}and{' '}
      <a href="https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Speed Insights privacy documentation</a>
      {' '}for their own, more detailed disclosures. Nothing collected here is sold,
      shared with advertisers, or used for anything beyond the purpose above.
    </p>

    <h2 class="section-heading">How long it's kept</h2>
    <p>
      Vercel guarantees Web Analytics and Speed Insights data for <strong>at least
      one month</strong> on this project's plan — Vercel's own retention may extend
      longer than that minimum. This site does not separately store, export, or
      retain any of this data itself.
    </p>

    <h2 class="section-heading">Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Because no cookie or identifier persists across visits, there is no
      per-visitor record this site (or Vercel, on its behalf) can look up, correct,
      or delete on request — the data collected is never linked back to a specific
      person. If you believe that's inaccurate, or have any other question, open an
      issue on{' '}
      <a href="https://github.com/sairam0424/daily-dose/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">this project's GitHub repository</a>.
      You also have the right to complain to your local data protection authority —
      in the UK, that's the{' '}
      <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Information Commissioner's Office (ICO)</a>.
    </p>
  </main>

  <SiteFooter />
</Layout>
